  "response_text": "The stack pool is a reserved block of memory used to store stacks for multiple threads. Instead of manually allocating stack space for each new thread, the OS can assign each thread a unique portion of the stack pool. This allows multiple threads to have their own separate stacks in a predictable way. In future labs, the stack pool makes it easy to dynamically create threads, since the OS can simply select an unused region from the pool, initialize it, and assign it to a new thread. This enables efficient thread management and supports scalability in a multi-threaded OS.\\n",
